It still renders as `Color.RED`. Annotating the parameter as `: Color` only constrains what you can pass; it doesn't change the member's string form. `f"{color}"` uses the enum member's default representation, which is `Color.RED` -- so `describe(Color.RED, Status.ACTIVE)` returns `Color: Color.RED, Status: Status.ACTIVE`, identical to before.

